  "_comment": [
    "Standard British-cryptic abbreviations: the one- to three-letter chunks a",
    "setter may drop into wordplay without signalling them further. Keys are",
    "uppercase letters; values are the lowercase clue words that stand for them.",
    "",
    "Derived from usage: every reading ten or more clues in",
    "tools/data/lexicons/blocks.json give (build_abbreviations.SEEN_MIN) is here,",
    "unless build_abbreviations.derived() shows it is two pieces or REJECT says",
    "why it is not one convention; `python3 tools/build_abbreviations.py --check`",
    "fails in CI on any it misses. Below that count a sense stays only as a member",
    "of a set solvers learn whole (build_abbreviations.FAMILIES, Roman numerals)",
    "or a textbook convention. Write it with tools/add_abbreviation.py, never by hand.",
    "",
    "tools/clueability.py uses these as legal charade and container pieces, and",
    "the site's hints and /abbreviations/ page teach them to solvers."
